ing statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $RP$ is well defined\n- The product $PS$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $P$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, $R$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $S$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{5\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $P$ and $5$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $P$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-22062/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22062"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-22055/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "070bbbb9-66be-54a2-9457-1f9270350e3a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22055/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "af0065fd-2614-5443-9593-e5c739f69ec4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22055/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "2aca32e8-7d3e-55d5-ab41-6bf0d2e7c610" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22055/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e003cc41-917b-5f03-bf99-0c9dd841a595" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22055/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "fa040ef8-ac8b-5437-b44c-cc48674960fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22055/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9cb8aeed-8720-58a3-9c27-db68e0ee00ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-22055/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-22055/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-22055/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-22055/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-22055/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-22055/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-22055" :question/id #uuid "016750b2-c60e-5605-864e-93f136cc483d" :question/math-academy-id "q-22055" :question/problem "$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $X,Y,$ and $Z?$\n\n- The product $XY$ is well defined\n- The product $YX$ is well defined\n- The product $YZ$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $X$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $Y$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $Z$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $X$ and $2$ rows in $Y.$ Since the number of columns in $X$ equals the number of rows in $Y,$ the matrices $X$ and $Y$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{X}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{Y}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $Y$ and $2$ rows in $X.$ Since the number of columns in $Y$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $X,$ the matrices $Y$ and $X$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{Y}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{X}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $Y$ and $3$ rows in $Z.$ Since the number of columns in $Y$ equals the number of rows in $Z,$ the matrices $Y$ and $Z$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{Y}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{Z}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-22055/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22055"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129437/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "30f910bd-709e-5567-9db8-b85b93ad6afe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129437/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f9304ac7-8bb9-54b8-8c7b-7370488ec631" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129437/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554b