es 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{P}_{5\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $5$ columns in $S$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement III is true, while statements I and II are false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129437/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129486/selection/67e2f68495bf59024298cc5a843e3c22980b8438c9ec5b0733bc7ed8ce150777" :answer/id #uuid "096cdb96-9de6-58c7-8667-5c74ea9b3486" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129486/selection/42764f37248aa873ad61f0036117fb1b57805a23423b4c03f00a55227ad68587" :answer/id #uuid "008c1879-9556-51a5-a9dc-077c78496cf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\times 7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129486/selection/c0a965fea66be2904113dd38a15852f0a4f0b4235e0ca765e68fd28773f7bab1" :answer/id #uuid "6f646e8b-6f9f-50fe-b6b7-64a7f9150698" :answer/type :answer.