eld/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129489/selection/f4b34d0646b6f3c53bfc3c7ce32e6a024b2a353a572afec0cdc6b99682fbad90" :answer-field/choices ["q-129489/selection/f4b34d0646b6f3c53bfc3c7ce32e6a024b2a353a572afec0cdc6b99682fbad90" "q-129489/selection/ffdfc66ecf145cc43a740857fb8c9a72e9d0dabd2314f553e752b06c72aad4cd" "q-129489/selection/67e2f68495bf59024298cc5a843e3c22980b8438c9ec5b0733bc7ed8ce150777" "q-129489/selection/d1e5d1b613abb74681f07a99cdb8bdd5c7f626faaa52929ed8fec80ebd4d62e0" "q-129489/selection/643eb390a5697a24eb83705ffb2417aea41c68638f4b77e44621c15f02d06b27"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129489" :question/id #uuid "445efc3b-d169-59e3-aea8-9ddc83b2ab13" :question/math-academy-id "q-129489" :question/problem "Let\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 8 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 4:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 4}={BA}_{2\\times 4}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-129489/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0a4fa3d-fc1a-5e95-a632-f3a25c9bc4b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129489"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4403"] :question/problem "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4404"] :question/worked-solution "There are $4$ columns in $A$ and $4$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication, and $AB$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{3} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{AB}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4405"] :question/problem "Let\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that $A$ is a $4 \\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2 \\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2 \\times 2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{4}}}{B} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{4}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{A} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{BA}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
